[size=5][b][color=#ffaa28]BL4 Save Editor[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]An offline, standalone save editor for Borderlands 4, in the spirit of Gibbed's Borderlands 2 editor.[/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lagarrueal/borderlands4-save-editor/main/docs/screenshots/backpack.png[/img]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Item editor[/b] for the backpack, equipped gear, bank and Lost Loot: weapons, heavy weapons, shields, ordnance, repkits, enhancements and class mods. See the item name, rarity, manufacturer, element, firmware, legendary red text and every part. Change any part from a searchable list limited to that slot, add or remove parts, change the level, favorite/junk, copy and paste item codes, duplicate, move between backpack and bank, or build a brand new item from any item type and rarity.
[*][b]Item stats[/b] computed from the game's own balance data and matching the in-game card (damage, accuracy, fire rate, magazine, reload time, DPS, elemental DPS, crit), plus the numbers in effect texts ("+40% Movement Speed").
[*][b]Item validity check[/b]: every item is checked against the game data. Items the game would reject (it hides them as "unknown items") are flagged as errors and you are asked before saving them; unusual combinations that cannot drop normally are flagged as warnings. Items that only exist with a mod installed are recognised.
[*][b]Item pictures[/b]: item-type art, manufacturer logos, element and firmware icons taken from the game.
[*][b]Scale to level[/b]: one click scales a single item, or the whole backpack/bank, to your character level.
[*][b]Character[/b]: name, level and XP (written exactly the way the game stores them), specialization level, difficulty, True Mode, spawn checkpoint.
[*][b]Currencies[/b]: cash, eridium, SDU tokens, Vault Card tokens, ammo.
[*][b]Ultimate Vault Hunter[/b]: unlock UVH 1 to 7 and choose the active UVH level.
[*][b]SDU upgrades[/b]: buy any SDU level, or all of them; unlock weapon slots 3-4, repkit, enhancement and class mod slots.
[*][b]Missions[/b]: complete the main story (using the game's own story-skip records), complete any mission set or mission, reset a set, and set the status of each objective (mission checkpoints).
[*][b]Appearance[/b]: change the equipped head, body, skin, ECHO-4 and vehicle cosmetics; unlock cosmetics per group or all at once (pre-order/premium/SHiFT items excluded unless you ask).
[*][b]Raw YAML[/b] view of the decrypted save for advanced edits, with undo/redo for everything.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Safety[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Your character and profile.sav are [b]backed up automatically the moment you open them[/b] (bl4editor_backups folder next to your saves).
[*]Saving is [b]blocked while Borderlands 4 is running[/b] - the game would overwrite your edits.
[*]Saves are written exactly like the game writes them: an unedited save comes back byte-for-byte identical.
[*]Before writing, the editor checks the save structure, and refuses to put more items in the backpack or bank than they hold (the game deletes the overflow).
[/list]

[size=4][b]How to use[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Quit Borderlands 4 completely.
[*]Turn off Steam Cloud for Borderlands 4 while you edit, or choose the local files if Steam asks afterwards.
[*]Run [b]BL4SaveEditor.exe[/b]. Your saves (Documents\My Games\Borderlands 4\Saved\SaveGames\<steamid>\Profiles\client) are found automatically.
[*]Pick a character on the left, edit, press [b]Save[/b] (Ctrl+S).
[/list]
To restore a backup, copy it from bl4editor_backups over the original N.sav / profile.sav and remove the date from its name.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
Windows 10/11 (64-bit). Nothing to install - a single exe. Works offline.

[size=4][b]Game updates[/b][/size]
The game data is built into the exe for the current game version. After a game patch adds new items, a new version of the editor (or a new bl4db.json.gz placed next to the exe) brings them in. Items it does not know yet are flagged, never deleted.

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/lagarrueal/borderlands4-save-editor]github.com/lagarrueal/borderlands4-save-editor[/url] (MIT). Bug reports and ideas welcome on the GitHub issues page.

[size=2]Borderlands 4 is a trademark of Gearbox Software / 2K. This tool is not affiliated with or endorsed by them. Edit at your own risk and keep backups; avoid using edited items in matchmaking with strangers.[/size]
